#%RAML 1.0 SecurityScheme
type: x-client-id-enforcement
description: |
  Client ID Enforcement, applied by API Manager (policy on this API's instance; the
  application pairs with it through API autodiscovery). Callers send the credentials of
  their client application, which needs an approved contract with this API. The
  application itself does not check them: where the API is not managed (locally, in
  tests) the headers are ignored.
describedBy:
  headers:
    client_id:
      type: string
      description: Client ID of the calling application.
    client_secret:
      type: string
      description: Client secret of the calling application.
  responses:
    401:
      description: Missing or invalid client credentials (answered by the policy).
